At least 2 GB of free RAM (inc. virtual) required for installing this repack","Driveclub is a 2014 racing video game developed by Evolution Studios and published by Sony Computer Entertainment exclusively for the PlayStation 4. Departing from the strict simulation of franchises like Gran Turismo, the game focuses on accessible arcade-style racing that still rewards precise handling and driving lines. Players compete across various real-world locations—including Chile, India, Japan, Norway, Scotland, and Canada—behind the wheel of a vast roster of meticulously detailed, licensed sports cars and hypercars.
The core experience revolves around the concept of clubs, allowing up to six players to band together to form cohesive racing teams. Within these clubs, members work collaboratively to complete distinct challenges, earn Accrued Fame points, and level up to unlock exclusive vehicles and rewards. The game seamlessly integrates synchronous and asynchronous multiplayer elements, constantly pushing real-time “Faceoffs” and dynamically generated community challenges onto the player’s screen, ensuring that every corner turned contributes to their team’s global standing.
Upon its initial launch, Driveclub suffered from severe server instability that overshadowed its release; however, subsequent updates transformed it into a critical success and a visual showcase for the PlayStation 4. The developers introduced an industry-leading dynamic weather system and an expansive photo mode that highlighted the game’s stunning graphical fidelity. Despite its eventual redemption and strong post-launch support, Sony officially shut down the game’s online servers in March 2020 and removed the title from digital storefronts, leaving it accessible today only through physical disc copies for offline play.",1
